"""Per-character advance widths for the three font stacks the SVGs use.

Measured, not estimated. The engine used to reach for Pillow and a DejaVu TTF, and fall
back to a flat 0.60 em per character when the file was missing. That fallback ran 40%
wide, which is harmless for a badge (it just gets extra padding) but wrecks prose: lines
broke a quarter early and the panel looked like a narrow column with a ragged edge.

Worse, it was machine-dependent. A CI runner has DejaVu and a Windows laptop does not, so
the same build produced different line breaks depending on where it ran, and these SVGs
are committed. A table in the repository removes that entirely.

Generated by measuring every printable ASCII character through a browser canvas at the
exact stacks declared in svg.py. Values are em fractions at weight 400, 500 and 700.
Platform fonts differ (Segoe UI here, SF on a Mac, Ubuntu on Linux), so callers that must
not overflow apply SAFETY on top.

Regenerate: measure the stacks in a browser and rewrite this file. Do not hand-edit.
"""

